violent animal attacks are all too real  while lots of elements of nope fall  squarely into the realm of science  fiction one plot line shares some  similarities to a real life horror story  here's how they line up spoilers for  nope ahead  jordan peele's latest film nope is out  in theaters and audiences finally know  what the film is actually about the  narrative exemplifies peel's signature  brand of storytelling examining themes  like the pursuit of fame the dark side  of exhibition and wild animals  relationship with humans it's an  adventure and a horror spectacle about  about human nature untameable beasts  play a significant role in the narrative  in more ways than one siblings o.j and  emerald haywood are struggling to  maintain their father's horse training  business after his mysterious death but  that's the least of their problems  thanks to their neighbor former child  actor and current theme park owner ricky  jupe park their property has  inadvertently become home base for a  flying extraterrestrial predator  flashbacks show that jup's fascination  with the wild creature is no coincidence  as a child he starred on a sitcom called  gordy's home which starred a live  chimpanzee alongside a group of human  actors one fateful day the primates  snapped and brutally mauled several  actors including jup's young co-star  mary jo elliott who miraculously  survived despite sustaining severe  injuries though viewers only see the  incident from jup's limited perspective  what we are shown is enough to imagine  the horror of what's happened this  section of the plot is particularly  alarming and specific so it makes sense  that gordy's violent outburst has some  clear parallels to a devastating true  story new york magazine reports that in  1995 sondra and jerome harold paid a  missouri-based breeder 50 000  in exchange for travis the chimpanzee  raising him from infancy travis  developed human qualities under their  care he got dressed every day brushed  his teeth enjoyed ice cream and wine and  even slept in bed with the couple  similar to gordy in nope travis was a  bit of a celebrity he was known for  appearing in old navy ads and local  businesses proudly displayed photographs  of him according to the stamford  advocate much like gordy travis existed  in a world where he was the center of  attention however there were warning  signs that travis might not be the  obedient pet he seemed to be the  stamford advocate also reports that the  chimpanzee pulled a woman's arm through  the opened window of a parked car in  1996 biting her hard enough to draw  blood in 2003 he jumped out of the  herald's car at an intersection evading  police and his owners for two hours at  that time no charges repressed according  to new york magazine a recurring motif  and nope is the dedication and respect  it takes to develop a connection with a  wild animal assuming obedience is a  recipe for disaster a mistake jup makes  at the cost of his life in travis's case  his perceived domestication likewise did  nothing to stop the inevitable in  february 2009 charla nash a friend of  sandra herald arrived to help care for  travis who is 14 years old and 200  pounds at the time he brutally attacked  her before being shot and killed by the  police the new york times reported  charla suffered extreme and extensive  injuries to her face and hands it's a  horrible thing but i'm not a horrible  person and he wasn't a horrible chimp  several months into her recovery charla  appeared on the oprah winfrey show to  talk about the traumatic experience for  most of the interview charla's face was  shielded by a veiled hat very similar to  the head covering we see an adult mary  jo wearing in nope when she attends  jup's alien demonstration all those  years after the gordy's home incident  although it hasn't been officially  confirmed that the gordy storyline in  nope was directly inspired by charla  nash's survival story some parallels are  clearly there of course unlike mary jo  who suffered another tragic fate nash's  condition has only improved over the  years she received a successful face  transplant in 2011 and according to abc7  has become an advocate for stricter  legislation regarding the sale of exotic  animals  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

